IMPORT prelude

-- Customs Act 1960 (Singapore) -- the traveller and the small importer: declaring at the border (s 93), the baggage,
-- possession and duty-free-allowance offences (ss 128E, 128I, 128J), the penalty scale (s 128L), the burden of proof and
-- presumptions (ss 93(4), 115, 115A, 128L(6)), unclaimed seizures (s 124), costs after a seizure (s 127), refunds and
-- short levies (ss 19, 20), and the fuel rule for vehicles leaving Singapore (s 136).
--
-- Edition: 2020 Revised Edition, informal consolidation, as deposited at ../../registers/source-bundle/ (amendments to
-- Act 6 of 2025).
--
-- WHY THIS ACT. Cited by 40 of the 527 Singapore Acts deposited in this repository (most often ss 3 and 4). SCOPED to
-- what a traveller or small importer meets. Not encoded: officers (Part 2), valuation and the levying machinery
-- (Part 3), import and export procedure (Part 4), vessels, warehousing, manufacture, drawback, duty-free shops and
-- composite licences (Parts 5 to 11), most of Part 12, search and arrest (Part 13), and the regulations. No duty rates
-- or allowances were retrieved; they are in subsidiary legislation.
--
-- NAIVE ENCODING. Straight from the deposited text with the writing-l4-rules skill. No pipeline, no coverage table,
-- no independent test pass, no human gate. See NOTES.md.

§ `Customs Act 1960 -- the traveller`

§§ `93 -- declaring at the border`

-- s 93(1), (2): every person arriving must declare (at the Red Channel where there is one) all dutiable goods that exceed
-- their duty-free allowance or for which none is granted, "and pay the ... duty ... before he or she proceeds".
-- (3): goods on which duty is not so paid "are deemed to be uncustomed goods". (4): a person who takes the GREEN channel
-- with such goods "is presumed, until the contrary is proved, to be in possession of uncustomed goods".
DECLARE Arrival HAS
    `carries dutiable goods beyond the allowance or with no allowance` IS A BOOLEAN
    `declared them at the Red Channel` IS A BOOLEAN
    `paid the duty before proceeding` IS A BOOLEAN
    `took the Green Channel` IS A BOOLEAN

GIVEN `the arrival` IS AN Arrival
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the goods are uncustomed` IF
        `the arrival`'s `carries dutiable goods beyond the allowance or with no allowance`
    AND NOT `the arrival`'s `paid the duty before proceeding`

GIVEN `the arrival` IS AN Arrival
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `possession of uncustomed goods is presumed` IF
        `the arrival`'s `carries dutiable goods beyond the allowance or with no allowance`
    AND `the arrival`'s `took the Green Channel`

§§ `128E, 128I, 128J -- the traveller's offences`

-- s 128E: "Any person who after he or she DENIES having, is found to have, any dutiable or prohibited goods in the
-- person's baggage or upon his or her person or otherwise in the person's possession shall be guilty of an offence."
-- s 128I(1)(a): storing, keeping or possessing dutiable or prohibited goods except under customs control, or uncustomed
-- goods.
-- s 128J: "Any person who sells, exchanges or GIVES AWAY, or offers to ... give away, to any person in Singapore goods which
-- are the person's duty-free allowances in Singapore shall be guilty of an offence."
-- s 128L(7): each is a "specified offence".
-- s 128L(6): in any prosecution under ss 128D to 128K, the goods "are deemed to be dutiable, uncustomed or prohibited goods
-- to the person's KNOWLEDGE, unless the contrary is proved".
--
-- s 128J reaches a gift. A traveller who brings in a duty-free bottle and gives it to a friend in Singapore commits a
-- specified offence, carrying the minimum fine below.
DECLARE TravellerConduct IS ONE OF
    `denying having dutiable goods that are then found`
    `possessing uncustomed goods`
    `selling duty-free allowance goods in Singapore`
    `giving duty-free allowance goods to a friend in Singapore`
    `consuming one's own duty-free allowance`
    `declaring and paying duty on excess goods`

GIVEN `the conduct` IS A TravellerConduct
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the conduct is a specified offence` IF
    CONSIDER `the conduct`
    WHEN `consuming one's own duty-free allowance` THEN FALSE
    WHEN `declaring and paying duty on excess goods` THEN FALSE
    OTHERWISE TRUE

§§ `128L -- the penalty scale for specified offences`

-- s 128L(2): a fine "(a) not less than 10 times the amount of the ... duty ... or $5,000, WHICHEVER IS THE LESSER
-- amount, subject to a minimum of $1,000 where the specified offence involves ... relevant tobacco products; and (b) not
-- more than 20 times the amount of the ... duty ... or $5,000, WHICHEVER IS THE GREATER amount"; where the duty cannot be
-- ascertained, a fine up to $10,000 (minimum $1,000 for tobacco). (2A): and up to 12 months.
-- (3), (3A): a repeat offender -- the same fine scale and up to 2 years.
-- (4): tobacco over 2 kg -- not less than 15 times the duty (minimum $1,000), not more than the greater of 20 times or
-- $10,000; or up to 3 years; or both.
--
-- The minimum fine is a mandatory floor. On $40 of duty evaded, the court must fine at least $400; on $1,000 evaded, at
-- least $5,000. For tobacco, the floor never falls below $1,000, so $10 of evaded duty on a pack of cigarettes carries a
-- minimum $1,000.
DECLARE Evasion HAS
    `duty evaded` IS A NUMBER
    `involves tobacco` IS A BOOLEAN
    `tobacco weight in kg` IS A NUMBER

GIVEN `p` IS A NUMBER, `q` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the lesser of` MEANS
    IF `p` LESS THAN `q` THEN `p` ELSE `q`

GIVEN `p` IS A NUMBER, `q` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the greater of` MEANS
    IF `p` GREATER THAN `q` THEN `p` ELSE `q`

GIVEN `the evasion` IS AN Evasion
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the heavy tobacco scale applies` IF
        `the evasion`'s `involves tobacco`
    AND `the evasion`'s `tobacco weight in kg` GREATER THAN 2

GIVEN `the evasion` IS AN Evasion
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the minimum fine` MEANS
    IF `the heavy tobacco scale applies` `the evasion`
    THEN `the greater of` (15 TIMES `the evasion`'s `duty evaded`) 1000
    ELSE IF `the evasion`'s `involves tobacco`
         THEN `the greater of` (`the lesser of` (10 TIMES `the evasion`'s `duty evaded`) 5000) 1000
         ELSE `the lesser of` (10 TIMES `the evasion`'s `duty evaded`) 5000

GIVEN `the evasion` IS AN Evasion
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the maximum fine` MEANS
    IF `the heavy tobacco scale applies` `the evasion`
    THEN `the greater of` (20 TIMES `the evasion`'s `duty evaded`) 10000
    ELSE `the greater of` (20 TIMES `the evasion`'s `duty evaded`) 5000

-- In months, first offence.
GIVEN `the evasion` IS AN Evasion
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the maximum imprisonment` MEANS
    IF `the heavy tobacco scale applies` `the evasion` THEN 36 ELSE 12

§§ `115, 115A -- burden of proof and presumptions`

-- s 115: in any prosecution about seized goods, a dispute whether duty was paid, the goods were lawfully imported, they
-- were exempt, where they came from, or whether drawback was lawfully claimed -- "the burden of proof thereof shall lie on
-- the defendant".
-- s 115A(1): a person with possession of a thing, its keys, the keys of premises where the goods are, or a document of
-- title, is presumed to possess the goods. (3): goods "found in any vehicle" are presumed to be in the possession "of the
-- OWNER of the vehicle AND of the person in charge of the vehicle for the time being".
--
-- s 115A(3) puts the owner of a car lent to a friend in presumed possession of contraband the friend carries.
DECLARE VehicleFind HAS
    `goods found in the vehicle` IS A BOOLEAN
    `is the owner` IS A BOOLEAN
    `is the person in charge` IS A BOOLEAN
    `rebutted the presumption` IS A BOOLEAN

GIVEN `the find` IS A VehicleFind
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the person is presumed to possess the goods` IF
        `the find`'s `goods found in the vehicle`
    AND (`the find`'s `is the owner` OR `the find`'s `is the person in charge`)
    AND NOT `the find`'s `rebutted the presumption`

DECLARE Dispute IS ONE OF
    `whether duty was paid`
    `whether the goods were lawfully imported`
    `whether the goods were exempt`
    `where the goods came from`
    `whether drawback was lawfully claimed`
    `whether the accused was present`

GIVEN `the dispute` IS A Dispute
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the defendant bears the burden on the dispute` IF
    CONSIDER `the dispute`
    WHEN `whether the accused was present` THEN FALSE
    OTHERWISE TRUE

§§ `124, 127 -- seized goods`

-- s 124(1): if there is no prosecution, seized goods "are to be taken and deemed to be forfeited at the expiry of ONE
-- MONTH from the date of seizure unless a claim thereto is made before that date". (6): in the court proceedings on a
-- claim, s 115 puts the burden on the claimant.
-- s 127: no costs, damages or other relief "other than an order for the return of the goods or the payment of their
-- value unless the seizure was made without reasonable or probable cause".
GIVEN `days since seizure` IS A NUMBER, `prosecuted` IS A BOOLEAN, `claimed in writing` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the goods are deemed forfeited` IF
        NOT `prosecuted`
    AND NOT `claimed in writing`
    AND `days since seizure` GREATER THAN 30

GIVEN `the seizure had reasonable or probable cause` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the owner may recover damages and costs` IF
    NOT `the seizure had reasonable or probable cause`

§§ `19, 20 -- refunds and short levies`

-- s 19(3)(a): a refund only if claimed "within 5 years after the overpayment". s 20(1A)(b): a demand for a short levy
-- must be made "within 5 years after the date of payment", but (1B): not if the short levy resulted from the payer's
-- fraud or evasion -- then there is no time limit.
GIVEN `years since overpayment` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the refund claim is in time` IF
    `years since overpayment` AT MOST 5

GIVEN `years since payment` IS A NUMBER, `fraud or evasion by the payer` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `a demand for the short levy is in time` IF
    `fraud or evasion by the payer` OR `years since payment` AT MOST 5

§§ `136 -- leaving with a near-empty tank`

-- s 136(1): a person in charge of a Singapore-registered motor vehicle who leaves or attempts to leave Singapore without
-- the minimum fuel the Minister prescribes -- fine up to $500. (2)(a): driving past the Customs gantry before the
-- departure bay is presumed an attempt to leave. (b): the fuel gauge is evidence of the amount. (3): permission may be
-- given after the attempt, "without affecting any liability ... for such attempt".
-- The prescribed minimum (the "three-quarter tank rule") is in an order not retrieved; it is a parameter here.
DECLARE Departure HAS
    `fuel as a fraction of the tank` IS A NUMBER
    `prescribed minimum fraction` IS A NUMBER
    `drove past the Customs gantry` IS A BOOLEAN
    `has written permission` IS A BOOLEAN
    `permission came after the attempt` IS A BOOLEAN

GIVEN `the departure` IS A Departure
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the driver commits the fuel offence` IF
        `the departure`'s `drove past the Customs gantry`
    AND `the departure`'s `fuel as a fraction of the tank` LESS THAN `the departure`'s `prescribed minimum fraction`
    AND (    NOT `the departure`'s `has written permission`
         OR  `the departure`'s `permission came after the attempt`)
